# Local dev env for `next dev`. Copy to `.env` and fill in.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# .env is gitignored — never put real secrets in a tracked file. The one
# exception is .env.production, which is committed on purpose: it only ever
# holds the PUBLIC Turnstile site key (safe to ship in browser JS). The
# matching secret key is never a file on disk in this repo at all — it's set
# directly as a Worker secret (`wrangler secret put TURNSTILE_SECRET`), and
# has no client-side counterpart.

# Public Turnstile site key, inlined into the browser bundle at build time.
# Cloudflare's published "always passes" test key is safe to use here for
# local dev: 1x00000000000000000000AA
NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=

# Worker-side dev secrets (used by `wrangler dev`, not by `next dev`) live in
# .dev.vars, not here — see README.md's secrets table for the full list
# (TURNSTILE_SECRET, INBOX_API_KEY) and their Cloudflare test-key equivalents.
